@.str.19 = private unnamed_addr constant [7084 x i8] c"\0A      Fetch a file system tree or a plain file using one of the supported backends and return an attribute set with:\0A\0A      - the resulting fixed-output [store path](@docroot@/glossary.md#gloss-store-path)\0A      - the corresponding [NAR](@docroot@/glossary.md#gloss-nar) hash\0A      - backend-specific metadata (currently not documented). <!-- TODO: document output attributes -->\0A\0A      *input* must be an attribute set with the following attributes:\0A\0A      - `type` (String, required)\0A\0A        One of the [supported source types](#source-types).\0A        This determines other required and allowed input attributes.\0A\0A      - `narHash` (String, optional)\0A\0A        The `narHash` parameter can be used to substitute the source of the tree.\0A        It also allows for verification of tree contents that may not be provided by the underlying transfer mechanism.\0A        If `narHash` is set, the source is first looked up is the Nix store and [substituters](@docroot@/command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-substituters), and only fetched if not available.\0A\0A      A subset of the output attributes of `fetchTree` can be re-used for subsequent calls to `fetchTree` to produce the same result again.\0A      That is, `fetchTree` is idempotent.\0A\0A      Downloads are cached in `$XDG_CACHE_HOME/nix`.\0A      The remote source will be fetched from the network if both are true:\0A      - A NAR hash is supplied and the corresponding store path is not [valid](@docroot@/glossary.md#gloss-validity), that is, not available in the store\0A\0A        > **Note**\0A        >\0A        > [Substituters](@docroot@/command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-substituters) are not used in fetching.\0A\0A      - There is no cache entry or the cache entry is older than [`tarball-ttl`](@docroot@/command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-tarball-ttl)\0A\0A      ## Source types\0A\0A      The following source types and associated input attributes are supported.\0A\0A      <!-- TODO: It would be soooo much more predictable to work with (and\0A      document) if `fetchTree` was a curried call with the first paramter for\0A      `type` or an attribute like `builtins.fetchTree.git`! -->\0A\0A      - `\22file\22`\0A\0A        Place a plain file into the Nix store.\0A        This is similar to [`builtins.fetchurl`](@docroot@/language/builtins.md#builtins-fetchurl)\0A\0A        - `url` (String, required)\0A\0A          Supported protocols:\0A\0A          - `https`\0A\0A            > **Example**\0A            >\0A            > ```nix\0A            > fetchTree {\0A            >   type = \22file\22;\0A            >   url = \22https://example.com/index.html\22;\0A            > }\0A            > ```\0A\0A          - `http`\0A\0A            Insecure HTTP transfer for legacy sources.\0A\0A            > **Warning**\0A            >\0A            > HTTP performs no encryption or authentication.\0A            > Use a `narHash` known in advance to ensure the output has expected contents.\0A\0A          - `file`\0A\0A            A file on the local file system.\0A\0A            > **Example**\0A            >\0A            > ```nix\0A            > fetchTree {\0A            >   type = \22file\22;\0A            >   url = \22file:///home/eelco/nix/README.md\22;\0A            > }\0A            > ```\0A\0A      - `\22tarball\22`\0A\0A        Download a tar archive and extract it into the Nix store.\0A        This has the same underyling implementation as [`builtins.fetchTarball`](@docroot@/language/builtins.md#builtins-fetchTarball)\0A\0A        - `url` (String, required)\0A\0A           > **Example**\0A           >\0A           > ```nix\0A           > fetchTree {\0A           >   type = \22tarball\22;\0A           >   url = \22https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/tarball/nixpkgs-23.11\22;\0A           > }\0A           > ```\0A\0A      - `\22git\22`\0A\0A        Fetch a Git tree and copy it to the Nix store.\0A        This is similar to [`builtins.fetchGit`](@docroot@/language/builtins.md#builtins-fetchGit).\0A\0A        - `url` (String, required)\0A\0A          The URL formats supported are the same as for Git itself.\0A\0A          > **Example**\0A          >\0A          > ```nix\0A          > fetchTree {\0A          >   type = \22git\22;\0A          >   url = \22git@github.com:NixOS/nixpkgs.git\22;\0A          > }\0A          > ```\0A\0A          > **Note**\0A          >\0A          > If the URL points to a local directory, and no `ref` or `rev` is given, Nix will only consider files added to the Git index, as listed by `git ls-files` but use the *current file contents* of the Git working directory.\0A\0A        - `ref` (String, optional)\0A\0A          A [Git reference](https://git-scm.com/book/en/v2/Git-Internals-Git-References), such as a branch or tag name.\0A\0A          Default: `\22HEAD\22`\0A\0A        - `rev` (String, optional)\0A\0A          A Git revision; a commit hash.\0A\0A          Default: the tip of `ref`\0A\0A        - `shallow` (Bool, optional)\0A\0A          Make a shallow clone when fetching the Git tree.\0A\0A          Default: `false`\0A\0A        - `submodules` (Bool, optional)\0A\0A          Also fetch submodules if available.\0A\0A          Default: `false`\0A\0A        - `allRefs` (Bool, optional)\0A\0A          If set to `true`, always fetch the entire repository, even if the latest commit is still in the cache.\0A          Otherwise, only the latest commit is fetched if it is not already cached.\0A\0A          Default: `false`\0A\0A        - `lastModified` (Integer, optional)\0A\0A          Unix timestamp of the fetched commit.\0A\0A          If set, pass through the value to the output attribute set.\0A          Otherwise, generated from the fetched Git tree.\0A\0A        - `revCount` (Integer, optional)\0A\0A          Number of revisions in the history of the Git repository before the fetched commit.\0A\0A          If set, pass through the value to the output attribute set.\0A          Otherwise, generated from the fetched Git tree.\0A\0A      The following input types are still subject to change:\0A\0A      - `\22path\22`\0A      - `\22github\22`\0A      - `\22gitlab\22`\0A      - `\22sourcehut\22`\0A      - `\22mercurial\22`\0A\0A     *input* can also be a [URL-like reference](@docroot@/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md#flake-references).\0A     The additional input types and the URL-like syntax requires the [`flakes` experimental feature](@docroot@/contributing/experimental-features.md#xp-feature-flakes) to be enabled.\0A\0A      > **Example**\0A      >\0A      > Fetch a GitHub repository using the attribute set representation:\0A      >\0A      > ```nix\0A      > builtins.fetchTree {\0A      >   type = \22github\22;\0A      >   owner = \22NixOS\22;\0A      >   repo = \22nixpkgs\22;\0A      >   rev = \22ae2e6b3958682513d28f7d633734571fb18285dd\22;\0A      > }\0A      > ```\0A      >\0A      > This evaluates to the following attribute set:\0A      >\0A      > ```nix\0A      > {\0A      >   lastModified = 1686503798;\0A      >   lastModifiedDate = \2220230611171638\22;\0A      >   narHash = \22sha256-rA9RqKP9OlBrgGCPvfd5HVAXDOy8k2SmPtB/ijShNXc=\22;\0A      >   outPath = \22/nix/store/l5m6qlvfs9sdw14ja3qbzpglcjlb6j1x-source\22;\0A      >   rev = \22ae2e6b3958682513d28f7d633734571fb18285dd\22;\0A      >   shortRev = \22ae2e6b3\22;\0A      > }\0A      > ```\0A\0A      > **Example**\0A      >\0A      > Fetch the same GitHub repository using the URL-like syntax:\0A      >\0A      >   ```nix\0A      >   builtins.fetchTree \22github:NixOS/nixpkgs/ae2e6b3958682513d28f7d633734571fb18285dd\22\0A      >   ```\0A    \00", align 1
